@startuml j6-shared-tickets
!include style.iuml
title J6 Shared tickets and the desk code
actor Staff
participant "Staff page\n(staff/index.html,\nstaff/staff.js, sync.js)" as SP
participant "api/health.js" as Health
participant "api/tickets.js" as Tix
database "Store (Postgres)\nthrough api/_store.js" as Store
participant "Patient chat on another device\n(chat.js, sync.js)" as Chat
actor Patient
autonumber

Staff -> SP : opens /staff
SP -> Health : sync.js: GET /api/health (no desk code typed yet)
Health --> SP : the store is "postgres"
SP --> Staff : this browser's tickets, and "Enter the desk code to see tickets from every device."
Staff -> SP : types the desk code and presses "Use code"
SP -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets (with the desk code)
Tix -> Tix : compares it with FRONTDESK_DESK_CODE
Tix -> Store : read the newest tickets of every device
Tix --> SP : the list
SP --> Staff : "<n> from other devices"; the queue shows them, urgent first
Patient -> Chat : asks a question on a phone
Chat -> Tix : sync.js: POST /api/tickets (the ticket, with that browser's key)
Tix -> Store : a row in the table tickets, owned by the hash of the key
SP -> Tix : sync.js: GET /api/tickets again, about every five seconds
Tix --> SP : the list, now with the new ticket
SP --> Staff : the new ticket appears in the queue
@enduml
